<!-- TAG: ch1_bg_of_the_study -->
## Background of the Study

<!-- UPDATE:START -->
The annual college admission testing process at the Ilocos Sur Polytechnic State College (ISPSC) Tagudin Campus operates without a unified digital platform, leaving the Registrar Office and the Guidance Office to manage their separate responsibilities through paper-based workflows and informal coordination. Responsibility boundaries between these offices are understood by convention rather than enforced by system controls: the Registrar Office manages application intake and issues admission slip
<!-- UPDATE:END -->
<!-- TAG: ch1_conceptual_framework -->
